      'I got this wrong in a specific way: I validated the transform against a sample I had chosen myself, and the sample contained no accounts with refunds issued in a different currency. I ran the job in one pass with no shadow write and no reversible step, because the window felt tight and I wanted to be the person who unblocked reporting. Finance found the corrupted rows nine days later. I owned the disclosure, wrote the reconstruction job, and rebuilt the affected rows from the event log over the following week rather than handing it off.',
