      'She had budget and needed to decide between funding more capacity or funding the rework, and my job was to give her enough understanding to choose rather than to make her trust me.',
    action:
      'I stopped using the words queue, worker and throughput. Instead I drew a single lane road with one toll booth and asked her what happens if we buy more cars, which she answered immediately and correctly. Then I marked the toll booth as our single writer to the ledger table and showed the nightly arrival graph next to it. She asked the right follow up question herself, which was how much the booth could be widened, and I gave her the two engineering estimates with their risks. I sent a half page written version afterwards so she could forward it without me.',
